#: lib/alnasl_web/live/help_live.ex:20
#, elixir-autogen, elixir-format
msgid "Alnasl reads the electronic boards in the hall, works out the moves from where the pieces stand, and sends moves and clock times to the results site. It keeps everything itself first, so a hall without internet loses nothing: what could not be sent goes out, in order, when the connection is back."
